# Maven build output, and nothing else.
#
# This module is a plain tracked directory in the umbrella checkout while every sibling is a git submodule
# carrying its own ignores, so without this line `git status --porcelain` at the repository root reports
# `?? backend/cash-account-modernized/target/` after the build the README mandates (`./mvnw -B clean verify`) -
# some 60 MB of build output that a blanket `git add -A` would commit, and a boundary-hygiene gate that can no
# longer tell this deliverable's files from its artifacts.
#
# Kept to this one pattern deliberately: a wider rule could hide a deliverable file from the same gate, which is
# the failure this file exists to prevent. The file itself is beyond AAP 0.2.1's frozen inventory and is recorded
# as row D5 of the README's authorization record.
target/
